Writing a page as markdown is linear in its length instead of quadratic. Verify-on-emit checked every candidate form by decoding the whole page so far; it now checks each against the block before it, then decodes the whole page once, and only if that does not read back exactly re-chooses the forms the old way. A 126-block docs page emits in ~1s instead of ~25s, which also stops the unit-test run timing out on CI.
